    featuredImagePrompt: "An editorial news layout featuring a split screen. On one side, a stylized depiction of the US Capitol Building with subtle red and blue political party colors merging and contrasting, symbolizing a divided government. On the other side, a subtle, abstract representation of geopolitical tension, perhaps a map silhouette of the Middle East with a faint, almost ethereal drone icon or subtle smoke effect, suggesting instability. The overall tone should be professional and informative, similar to a Bloomberg or Reuters news graphic, with clean lines and financial market elements like subtle upward-trending stock charts integrated into the political side, and a warning symbol on the geopolitical side. Avoid any literal depiction of violence or specific political figures. The composition should convey both legislative stability and external risk.",
