      tokenUtility: "Bitcoin (BTC) serves primarily as a decentralized digital currency, a store of value, and a medium of exchange. Its utility is derived from its scarcity, security via blockchain technology, and global acceptance. BNB\'s utility within the Binance ecosystem includes reduced trading fees, staking rewards, participation in Launchpad token sales, and being the gas token for transactions on the BNB Chain.",
      tokenomics: "Bitcoin (BTC) has a capped supply of 21 million coins, ensuring scarcity. Its issuance rate halves approximately every four years (halving event), contributing to its deflationary model. The theft does not alter Bitcoin\'s fundamental tokenomics, but the movement of stolen coins can temporarily affect market dynamics. BNB has a deflationary mechanism through quarterly token burns, with its supply decreasing over time.",
