      neutralCase: "The crypto market will likely continue its trajectory of balancing innovation with increasing regulatory demands and security challenges. Periods of rapid growth will be interspersed with corrections driven by regulatory actions or security breaches. The industry will gradually mature, with compliant and secure solutions gaining prominence, while less compliant or insecure projects face marginalization.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "A probability-weighted outlook suggests a \'Neutral-to-Cautiously Bullish\' scenario. While significant headwinds from regulatory scrutiny and security threats persist, the underlying innovation and increasing efforts to address these issues (e.g., X\'s lawsuit, Ledger\'s transparency) point towards a more mature and potentially more stable, albeit slower, growth trajectory. The probability of widespread regulatory bans or catastrophic security failures leading to market collapse is relatively low, but localized impacts are high.",
      potentialCatalysts: ["Development of widely adopted, regulatory-compliant privacy solutions.", "Significant advancements in hardware wallet security and user education.", "Successful legal precedents against crypto fraud, enhancing market integrity.", "Clearer global regulatory frameworks for digital assets.", "Increased institutional investment in secure and compliant crypto products."],
      keyRisks: ["Unfavorable regulatory rulings or outright bans on privacy technologies.", "Major, widespread hardware wallet exploits leading to substantial financial losses.", "Persistent and evolving social media scams eroding public trust.", "Lack of global regulatory harmonization creating market fragmentation.", "Geopolitical events impacting digital asset markets and regulations."],
